# Line endings are a correctness concern in this repo, not a style preference.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default, so a Windows
# clone would rewrite install.sh into the working tree with CRLF. bash then
# fails on the first line with `$'\r': command not found` — before any of the
# installer's own Windows handling is even reached. The same conversion would
# break the doc-drift hook, which Claude Code executes directly.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree on every platform is the fix. Both files are
# read by interpreters that treat CR as content, never by Notepad.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.fragment text eol=lf
